<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Appendix A</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Preliminary</span>. The main mechanism that makes the transformer so effective is the Scaled Dot-Product Attention. Let’s say that our model has a dimensionality of <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, so each word embedding will be represented with a <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional vector. So, token embedding <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> will be represented as a vector <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. A sequence of <math id="A1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> tokens will be represented as <math id="A1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{S}_{N}=\{w_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝕊</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{S}_{N}=\{w_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> and their corresponding embeddings will be <math id="A1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=\mathbb{E}_{N}=\{\mathbf{x}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}\ \mathbf{x}_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=\mathbb{E}_{N}=\{\mathbf{x}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}\ \mathbf{x}_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The attention between two tokens <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is key and value and <math id="A1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> is the query will be</p>
<table id="A1.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Attention}(q_{m},k_{n},v_{n})=\mathrm{softmax}(\frac{\mathbf{q}_{m}\mathbf{k}_{n}^{T}}{\sqrt{d}})\mathbf{v}_{n}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Attention</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐤</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Attention}(q_{m},k_{n},v_{n})=\mathrm{softmax}(\frac{\mathbf{q}_{m}\mathbf{k}_{n}^{T}}{\sqrt{d}})\mathbf{v}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Where</p>
<table id="A1.E7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E7X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{q}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{q}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=f_{q}(\mathbf{x}_{m})=W_{q}x_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=f_{q}(\mathbf{x}_{m})=W_{q}x_{m}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="4" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E7Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{k}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐤</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{k}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=f_{k}(\mathbf{x}_{n})=W_{k}x_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=f_{k}(\mathbf{x}_{n})=W_{k}x_{n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E7Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{v}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{v}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=f_{v}(\mathbf{x}_{n})=W_{v}x_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=f_{v}(\mathbf{x}_{n})=W_{v}x_{n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E7Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E7Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{t:t\in\{q,k,v\}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{t:t\in\{q,k,v\}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The attention for the whole sequence will be</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Attention}(Q,K,V)=\mathrm{softmax}(\frac{QK^{T}}{\sqrt{d_{k}}})V" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Attention</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Attention}(Q,K,V)=\mathrm{softmax}(\frac{QK^{T}}{\sqrt{d_{k}}})V</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Where</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E9X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E9X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E9X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=f_{q}(\mathbf{x})=W_{q}\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=f_{q}(\mathbf{x})=W_{q}\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="4" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E9Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E9Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle K</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E9Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=f_{k}(\mathbf{x})=W_{k}\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=f_{k}(\mathbf{x})=W_{k}\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E9Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E9Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E9Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=f_{v}(\mathbf{x})=W_{v}\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=f_{v}(\mathbf{x})=W_{v}\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E9Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E9Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{t:t\in\{q,k,v\}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{t:t\in\{q,k,v\}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p7.3" class="ltx_p">The fact that all the computations are to be done in parallel means that the mechanism has no positional information about where the tokens are in the sequence. So, for the encoder model, if we don’t give the mechanism positional information. For decoder-only models <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Haviv et al. (2022)</a></cite> showed that the causative nature of the attention mechanism can create an internal representation of the positional information, but adding positional information still significantly improves the model performance. So, for us to encode the positional information in the embeddings, we need to redefine <math id="A1.p7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f_{t:t\in\{q,k,v\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{t:t\in\{q,k,v\}}</annotation></semantics></math> to take one more argument of the token position and to somehow encode it into the embedding.</p>
<table id="A1.E10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E10X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E10X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{q}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{q}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E10X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=f_{q}(\mathbf{x}_{m},m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=f_{q}(\mathbf{x}_{m},m)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E10Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E10Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{k}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐤</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{k}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E10Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=f_{k}(\mathbf{x}_{n},n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=f_{k}(\mathbf{x}_{n},n)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E10Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E10Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{v}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{v}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E10Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=f_{v}(\mathbf{x}_{n},n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=f_{v}(\mathbf{x}_{n},n)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p7.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{q}_{m},\mathbf{k}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐤</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{q}_{m},\mathbf{k}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> incorporate the <math id="A1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{th}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{th}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{th}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{th}</annotation></semantics></math> positions through <math id="A1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{q},f_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{q},f_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{v}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. The query and key values are then used to compute the attention weights, while the output is computed as the weighted sum over the value representation.</p>
<table id="A1.E11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E11X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E11X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle a_{m,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle a_{m,n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E11X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\exp(\frac{\mathbf{q}_{m}^{\intercal}\mathbf{k}_{n}}{\sqrt{d}})}{\sum_{j=1}^{N}\exp(\frac{\mathbf{q}_{m}^{\intercal}\mathbf{k}_{j}}{\sqrt{d}})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>⊺</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐤</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>⊺</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐤</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\exp(\frac{\mathbf{q}_{m}^{\intercal}\mathbf{k}_{n}}{\sqrt{d}})}{\sum_{j=1}^{N}\exp(\frac{\mathbf{q}_{m}^{\intercal}\mathbf{k}_{j}}{\sqrt{d}})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E11Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E11Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{o}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐨</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{o}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E11Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{n=1}^{N}a_{m,n}\mathbf{v}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{n=1}^{N}a_{m,n}\mathbf{v}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Learned Absolute position embedding</span>
One of the first methods proposed by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Vaswani et al. (2017)</a></cite> is</p>
<table id="A1.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f_{t:t\in\{q,k,v\}}(\mathbf{x}_{i},i):=\mathbf{W}_{t:t\in\{q,k,v\}}(\mathbf{x}_{i}+e_{i})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{t:t\in\{q,k,v\}}(\mathbf{x}_{i},i):=\mathbf{W}_{t:t\in\{q,k,v\}}(\mathbf{x}_{i}+e_{i}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p8.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is a d-dimensional embedding vector that is a learnable. The vector depends on the position of a token <math id="A1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. The approach was proposed and tried by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Vaswani et al. (2017)</a></cite>. They demonstrated that it is capable of learning to represent positional information, but it has several disadvantages.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">One is that the model can’t be used for inference on sequences longer than the ones it was trained on, since first, they don’t exist, and second, even if we created new embeddings in the position embeddings, they still would need to be trained.
Another significant disadvantage is that the new parameters increase the model’s size and the computational requirements during training.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">Learned Absolute position embeddings were used by BERT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Devlin et al. (2019)</a></cite>. While back then <math id="A1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="512" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>512</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">512</annotation></semantics></math> tokens context length was a standard in recent years, a lot of models like llama 3<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dubey et al. (2024)</a></cite> have a context length of <math id="A1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="128000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>128000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">128000</annotation></semantics></math> tokens, so for example for llama 3 <math id="A1.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math>B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dubey et al. (2024)</a></cite>. The use of such embeddings would add 0.5 billion training parameters.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sinusoidal Absolute position embedding</span>. One would believe that there should be a method to give the model the information needed to infer the token’s positions without the model needing to learn them. The approach <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Vaswani et al. (2017)</a></cite> preferred is</p>
<table id="A1.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f_{t:t\in\{q,k,v\}}(\mathbf{x}_{i},i):=\mathbf{W}_{t:t\in\{q,k,v\}}(\mathbf{x}_{i}+\mathbf{p}_{i})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{t:t\in\{q,k,v\}}(\mathbf{x}_{i},i):=\mathbf{W}_{t:t\in\{q,k,v\}}(\mathbf{x}_{i}+\mathbf{p}_{i}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p11.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{p}_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is a d-dimensional vector depending of the position of token <math id="A1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> in the sequence. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Vaswani et al. (2017)</a></cite> have proposed to generate <math id="A1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{p}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> using the sinusoidal function.</p>
<table id="A1.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{cases}\mathbf{p}_{i,2t}&amp;=\sin(i/10000^{2t/d})\\
\mathbf{p}_{i,2t+1}&amp;=\cos(i/10000^{2t/d})\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mn>10000</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mn>10000</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{cases}\mathbf{p}_{i,2t}&amp;=\sin(i/10000^{2t/d})\\
\mathbf{p}_{i,2t+1}&amp;=\cos(i/10000^{2t/d})\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p11.3" class="ltx_p">in which <math id="A1.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{p}_{i,2t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}_{i,2t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="A1.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2t^{th}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2t^{th}</annotation></semantics></math> element of the d-dimensional vector <math id="A1.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{p}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{p}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
While this method didn’t add any new parameters to the model, it still suffered from the model’s inability to extrapolate to sequences longer than those seen during training.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Relative position embeddings</span>. Both sinusoidal and learned position encodings focused on the absolute position of the token. Relative positional embeddings rely on a different approach, mainly the idea that the exact position of the word in the sequence is not relevant. What is essential is the word’s position relative to other words.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p13.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p13.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Rotary Position Embedding (RoPE)</span>. One of the most popular approaches is RoPE (Rotary Position Embeddings) proposed by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Su et al. (2023)</a></cite>. The approach is a relative positional embeddings method that again adds positional information to the query and key dot-product (<math id="A1.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{q}_{m}^{\intercal}\mathbf{k}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>⊺</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐤</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{q}_{m}^{\intercal}\mathbf{k}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>) values. To incorporate relative position information, it is required that the inner product of the query and key dot-product (<math id="A1.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{q}_{m}^{\intercal}\mathbf{k}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>⊺</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐤</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{q}_{m}^{\intercal}\mathbf{k}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>) values be formulated by a function <math id="A1.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>,
which takes only the word embeddings <math id="A1.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, and their relative position <math id="A1.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m-n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m-n</annotation></semantics></math> as input variables. They propose that the query and key dot-product (<math id="A1.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{q}_{m}^{\intercal}\mathbf{k}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>⊺</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐤</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{q}_{m}^{\intercal}\mathbf{k}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>) values encode their position information only in the relative form:</p>
<table id="A1.E15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E15X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle\mathbf{q}_{m},\mathbf{k}_{n}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐤</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle\mathbf{q}_{m},\mathbf{k}_{n}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\langle f_{q}(\mathbf{x}_{m},m),f_{k}(\mathbf{x}_{n},n)\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\langle f_{q}(\mathbf{x}_{m},m),f_{k}(\mathbf{x}_{n},n)\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E15Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=g(\mathbf{x}_{m},\mathbf{x}_{n},m-n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=g(\mathbf{x}_{m},\mathbf{x}_{n},m-n)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p14.1" class="ltx_p">They achieve this by applying a rotation matrix to the query and key tensors, which rotates the vectors relative to their position in the sequence.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p15" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E16X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{q}_{m}^{\intercal}\mathbf{k}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>⊺</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐤</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{q}_{m}^{\intercal}\mathbf{k}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(\mathbf{R}^{d}_{\Theta,m}\mathbf{W}_{q}\mathbf{x}_{m})^{\intercal}(\mathbf{R}^{d}_{\Theta,n}\mathbf{W}_{k}\mathbf{x}_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐑</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊺</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐑</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(\mathbf{R}^{d}_{\Theta,m}\mathbf{W}_{q}\mathbf{x}_{m})^{\intercal}(\mathbf{R}^{d}_{\Theta,n}\mathbf{W}_{k}\mathbf{x}_{n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E16Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbf{x}^{\intercal}\mathbf{W}_{q}R^{d}_{\Theta,n-m}\mathbf{W}_{k}\mathbf{x}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⊺</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbf{x}^{\intercal}\mathbf{W}_{q}R^{d}_{\Theta,n-m}\mathbf{W}_{k}\mathbf{x}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p15.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{R}^{d}_{\Theta,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐑</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{R}^{d}_{\Theta,i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the said <math id="A1.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional rotation matrix and <math id="A1.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{R}^{d}_{\Theta,n-m}=(\mathbf{R}^{d}_{\Theta,m})^{\intercal}\mathbf{R}^{d}_{\Theta,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐑</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐑</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊺</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐑</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{R}^{d}_{\Theta,n-m}=(\mathbf{R}^{d}_{\Theta,m})^{\intercal}\mathbf{R}^{d}_{\Theta,n}</annotation></semantics></math>. The rotation matrix has two parameters <math id="A1.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta</annotation></semantics></math>, which is a pre-defined, non-zero constant (a common default value is <math id="A1.p15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10,000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10,000</annotation></semantics></math>) that serves as a base for calculating the rotation angles applied to query and key vectors. The other parameter of the rotation matrix is the index of the token in the sequence. RoPE is currently the state-of-the-art positional embedding method for transformer-based models used in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Touvron et al. (2023b)</a></cite><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dubey et al. (2024)</a></cite><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">DeepSeek-AI et al. (2025)</a></cite><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Qwen et al. (2025)</a></cite><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al. (2025a)</a></cite>, although some of them use some techniques to help the extrapolation of the RoPE context length, like Dual Chunk
Attention <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">An et al. (2024)</a></cite> or Position Interpolation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al. (2023)</a></cite>. Different methods have extrapolation abilities, but they haven’t seen wide adoption like <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Press et al. (2022)</a></cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Raffel et al. (2023)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Appendix B</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Training parameters for the small-scale models in section <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Experiments and Evaluation of Causal Language Modeling ‣ 4 Experiments and Results ‣ ExPe: Exact Positional Encodings for Generative Transformer Models with Extrapolating Capabilities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> are shown in Table <a href="#A2.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Appendix B Appendix B ‣ ExPe: Exact Positional Encodings for Generative Transformer Models with Extrapolating Capabilities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T5" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A2.T5.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A2.T5.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T5.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="A2.T5.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Parameter</span></th>
<th id="A2.T5.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A2.T5.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Values</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A2.T5.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T5.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt">effective batch size</th>
<td id="A2.T5.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_right ltx_border_tt"><math id="A2.T5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="512" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>512</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">512</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T5.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T5.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">batch size</th>
<td id="A2.T5.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_right"><math id="A2.T5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>64</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">64</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T5.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T5.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">gradient accumulation steps</th>
<td id="A2.T5.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_right"><math id="A2.T5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T5.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T5.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">peak learning rate</th>
<td id="A2.T5.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_right"><math id="A2.T5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1e-3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1e-3</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T5.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T5.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">end learning rate</th>
<td id="A2.T5.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_right"><math id="A2.T5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3e-6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3e-6</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T5.2.7" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T5.2.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">optimizer</th>
<td id="A2.T5.2.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_right">AdamW</td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T5.2.8" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T5.2.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">optimizer <math id="A2.T5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A2.T5.2.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_right"><math id="A2.T5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.9</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.9</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T5.2.9" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T5.2.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">optimizer <math id="A2.T5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A2.T5.2.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_right"><math id="A2.T5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.95" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.95</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.95</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T5.2.10" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T5.2.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">weight decay</th>
<td id="A2.T5.2.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_right"><math id="A2.T5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T5.2.11" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T5.2.11.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">warm-up ratio</th>
<td id="A2.T5.2.11.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_right"><math id="A2.T5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10\%</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T5.2.12" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T5.2.12.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb">precision</th>
<td id="A2.T5.2.12.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb">fp<math id="A2.T5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>32</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">32</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
