<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 7: </span>Ablation studies done on ExPE. Here, for all models, the training length is 512 tokens. Where ExPE (p is stable) means we override with <math id="A2.T7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i},p_{i},..,p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i},p_{i},..,p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> instead of <math id="A2.T7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i},p_{i+1},..,p_{i+l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i},p_{i+1},..,p_{i+l}</annotation></semantics></math>. ExPE (<math id="A2.T7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l=1</annotation></semantics></math>) uses <math id="A2.T7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l=1</annotation></semantics></math> for it’s positional encodings. ExPE (once) has its positional encodings applied only once before the first transformer block. ExPE (learned initialized) has its positional encodings <math id="A2.T7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.T7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> parameters learned but initialized with the same values as the non learned variant. ExPE (learned) has its positional encodings <math id="A2.T7.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.T7.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> parameters learned.
</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A2.F2" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.19569v1/images/ExPe_example.png" id="A2.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:534/88;" width="534" height="88" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 2: </span>Flowchart showing when ExPE is applied in self-attention. ExPE gets applied to the input. Here, we assume self-attention, i.e., the Query, Key, and Value matrices are identical. </figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The train, dev, and test data split for the experiments in section <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Experiments and Evaluation of Causal Language Modeling ‣ 4 Experiments and Results ‣ ExPe: Exact Positional Encodings for Generative Transformer Models with Extrapolating Capabilities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> are <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="600,000,000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>600,000,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">600,000,000</annotation></semantics></math> training tokens and <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50,000,000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>50,000,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50,000,000</annotation></semantics></math> val/test, all with an average length of <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8,000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8,000</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Appendix C</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The list of model parameters mentioned in the large-scale experiments section <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Large-scale Experiments ‣ 4 Experiments and Results ‣ ExPe: Exact Positional Encodings for Generative Transformer Models with Extrapolating Capabilities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a> can be found in table <a href="#A3.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ Appendix C Appendix C ‣ ExPe: Exact Positional Encodings for Generative Transformer Models with Extrapolating Capabilities" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T8" class="ltx_table">
